1
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:22,430
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

2
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:22,480
(No, It Can't!!)

3
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:35,490
The Scent of Cherry Sage

4
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:35,910
So you solve for this double root by...

5
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,910
<i>No way this goes over well.</i>

6
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:39,030
I'll stay the night, too!

7
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,430
<i>Technically, it's Himari's place, but...</i>

8
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:43,720
<i>Spending the night with a guy?</i>

9
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,430
<i>Besides, there's that one issue...</i>

10
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:49,290
<i>What should I bring?</i>

11
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:51,080
<i>Are you serious about this?</i>

12
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,380
<i>Don't you need your mom's permission?</i>

13
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:56,920
<i>Does she even know I'll be there?</i>

14
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:07,140
No prob!

15
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:05,220
<i>Mom said it's fine since you're a good guy.</i>

16
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,570
<i>Come on, Mom!</i>

17
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,130
<i>Sensei!</i>

18
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:13,190
<i>This flunky's flirting 
with Enocchi during class!</i>

19
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,850
<i>Who said it was Enomoto-san?</i>

20
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:23,030
<i>Nice try. She just texted me 
about staying the night, too.</i>

21
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:25,750
<i>Really? Is she that excited to sleep over?</i>

22
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:29,950
<i>We've got a problem. 
No studying at my place today!</i>

23
00:02:30,410 --> 00:02:31,210
<i>What? Why not?</i>

24
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:33,880
<i>I told Onii-chan that Enocchi was coming,</i>

25
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:38,470
<i>and he went off about not letting 
Enomoto DNA step foot on our property.</i>

26
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:42,050
<i>Hibari-san really hates 
Enomoto-san's sister that much?</i>

27
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:43,680
<i>Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!</i>

28
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:45,720
<i>Then how about a family restaurant?</i>

29
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:49,610
<i>If any teachers see us out late, 
we'll get written up.</i>

30
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:50,660
<i>You're right.</i>

31
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,480
<i>You know, Yu.</i>

32
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,200
<i>You get pretty frantic 
when it comes to Enocchi.</i>

33
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:56,950
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

34
00:02:56,950 --> 00:02:59,200
<i>She's only trying to help out.</i>

35
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,660
<i>Hmm.</i>

36
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:01,520
<i>Really?</i>

37
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:05,160
<i>You sure you weren't hoping 
for a repeat of last night?</i>

38
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:08,480
Like hell I am!

39
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,290
Natsume!

40
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,800
You've got the nerve to play 
around on your smartphone in class?!

41
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,210
After we agreed to let you retake the exams?!

42
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,850
I-I'm sorry.

43
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:22,720
Bwa-ha!

44
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:26,220
Hey, there's Natsume-kun!

45
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:30,310
Hey, so we were talking with Himari-san.

46
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,890
Huh? What?

47
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,520
It's about this account!

48
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:35,490
Hang on, do you not remember us?

49
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:37,520
We were in the same class last year.

50
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,540
This!

51
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:41,150
"You" is actually Natsume-kun, right?

52
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:44,730
<i>Oh yeah, Himari said something about a leak.</i>

53
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:48,290
Um, well, even if it were actually me—

54
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:49,800
Which means?

55
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,560
It's totally true!

56
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,340
I knew Himari-san was hiding something!

57
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:57,050
Can I help you with something?

58
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,170
Can you make us accessories, too?

59
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:01,660
We have a friend who really wants one!

60
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:06,290
U-Umm, well, I'm kinda busy 
studying for a retake...

61
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,010
You're retaking the exams?

62
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:11,270
You seem so smart, though!

63
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,430
Natsu!

64
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,720
What are you doing with these commoners?

65
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,990
Hey, Makishima.

66
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:21,660
Shoo! He's mine. Go on, now.

67
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:22,840
Get real!

68
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,770
See ya, Natsume-kun!

69
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:25,920
See ya.

70
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:29,390
Let's go before his womanizer 
virus rubs off on us!

71
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:30,280
For sure!

72
00:04:30,790 --> 00:04:32,740
Um, what's up?

73
00:04:33,110 --> 00:04:36,880
I just wanted to ask what I should bring 
for the sleepover tonight.

74
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:39,200
Oh right, that...

75
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:41,360
<i>I thought she was never 
speaking to me again.</i>

76
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:44,400
<i>But she seems back to normal.</i>

77
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,680
<i>Maybe she forgot with 
the whole sleepover thing?</i>

78
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:50,890
U-Um, actually, I've been 
meaning to tell you...

79
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:55,850
We can't study at my place today.

80
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,810
Oh, okay...

81
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:05,730
You've sure made a name for yourself, Natsu.

82
00:05:05,970 --> 00:05:10,020
Himari told me you're the reason 
for the leak to begin with.

83
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,250
I sure am.

84
00:05:12,110 --> 00:05:14,420
You could at least feel guilty about it.

85
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,720
Never mind that.

86
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,200
Could you help convince Enomoto-san for me?

87
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:21,240
Convince her? Of what?

88
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:28,500
So she's spending the night with 
her crush under the pretext of studying.

89
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,830
Pretty bold of Rin-chan.

90
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:40,890
I must say, I'm proud as her 
childhood friend and romance advisor.

91
00:05:41,730 --> 00:05:44,530
We're not spending the night, 
it's a study group.

92
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,760
Himari will be there, too.

93
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,120
Wait, so you didn't tell her to do that?

94
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:50,440
It's the first I've heard of it.

95
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:53,750
I did tell her to be assertive 
since you're easily pressured.

96
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:55,100
You idiot!

97
00:05:55,970 --> 00:05:57,440
Is that a problem?

98
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:01,110
The girl you love 
and the girl who loves you.

99
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,920
A thrilling sleepover 
caught between the two.

100
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:09,880
I've never experienced that, 
even when I had five girlfriends.

101
00:06:11,110 --> 00:06:14,600
Natsu, you must be the star of a rom-com.

102
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:17,110
Stop jabbering and help me out here.

103
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:18,040
Not my problem.

104
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,840
Do whatever you want.

105
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,850
These are the consequences for your actions.

106
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,240
I know you were getting handsy with

107
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:29,000
Himari-chan in 
the science room the other day.

108
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,610
H-How do you know that?

109
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,360
Don't make me tell you.

110
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:36,840
You should have at least locked the doors.

111
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,570
Wh-Who was watching? Enomoto-san?

112
00:06:40,570 --> 00:06:41,920
Anyways...

113
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,980
Have fun screwing this up!

114
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:48,750
<i>So no help from Makishima.</i>

115
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:51,860
<i>How am I gonna convince Enomoto-san now?</i>

116
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:53,910
Yu!

117
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,290
About the study group tonight.

118
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,720
We can have it at your place, right?

119
00:06:57,890 --> 00:06:58,640
What?

120
00:06:58,990 --> 00:07:00,920
Well we can't have it at my place.

121
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:03,750
And anywhere public's a no-go.

122
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:07,110
So it's gotta be your place!

123
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:09,100
No way.

124
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:11,950
You're one thing, but there's no way 
I can let Enomoto-san stay the night.

125
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:13,950
I mean—neither of you can stay!

126
00:07:13,950 --> 00:07:17,440
Come on, you can make up 
an excuse about the sleepover.

127
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,940
I'll be there, too.

128
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:20,420
I dunno...

129
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,680
Enocchi's really excited for it, you know?

130
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:27,110
And I accidentally told her 
we'd do it at your place.

131
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:28,570
Please!

132
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:32,090
I felt so bad my place got nixed 
at the last minute.

133
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:35,000
So... Please?

134
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:38,560
<i>Dammit... She's... too cute!</i>

135
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:40,560
Himari-san!

136
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,470
'Sup?

137
00:07:41,470 --> 00:07:43,730
We've got Student Council 
after school today.

138
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:44,700
Okay!

139
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:45,150
What?

140
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:46,650
Wait, Himari!

141
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:47,580
Sorry, Yu.

142
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:49,940
I totally forgot about Student Council.

143
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:52,160
You two get started without me!

144
00:07:53,330 --> 00:07:55,880
Don't worry! I'll get it over 
with in no time!

145
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,170
You've gotta be kidding...

146
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,210
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

147
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,340
Why is it like this today of all days?

148
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:17,050
First thing's first! Gotta start cleaning!

149
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:23,320
There. That should do it.

150
00:08:24,030 --> 00:08:27,310
<i>Now I just have to make sure 
Saku-nee-san doesn't see Enomoto-san.</i>

151
00:08:31,290 --> 00:08:32,160
Come on in!

152
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:42,080
Hello.

153
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:43,600
W-Welcome.

154
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:45,800
Come on inside.

155
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,280
Thanks for having me.

156
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:51,210
<i>Her outfit's so cute.</i>

157
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:53,300
<i>And she wore my hair pin.</i>

158
00:08:54,810 --> 00:08:56,890
No one's here, so make yourself at home.

159
00:08:58,090 --> 00:08:58,850
Really?

160
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,370
They're all at the store across the street.

161
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:04,480
My family owns it. 
I work there sometimes, too.

162
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:09,980
Th-Then it's just us 
until Hii-chan comes over?

163
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,810
Something the matter?

164
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,800
Nothing, just...

165
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,320
There's no flowers.

166
00:09:21,570 --> 00:09:23,280
Oh, right.

167
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,240
I store them here so Daifuku 
doesn't get into them.

168
00:09:27,110 --> 00:09:29,460
Some flowers are toxic to cats.

169
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:32,920
Wow, Yu-kun. It's like a world for fairies.

170
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:34,700
What's this called?

171
00:09:34,890 --> 00:09:35,830
That's cherry sage.

172
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:40,170
They're known as herbs, 
but the flowers have a relaxing scent.

173
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:44,080
So I like to keep them out 
when I'm studying or playing games.

174
00:09:44,690 --> 00:09:47,560
Wow. So you made it both 
beautiful and practical.

175
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:51,320
S-Sure, not that I came up with it.

176
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,100
All right then. Let me start 
with a review of yesterday.

177
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:58,690
Enomoto-san, can you 
help me if I get stuck?

178
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:01,760
Totally. I think I can go over most topics.

179
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,630
I'm actually second in our class.

180
00:10:03,830 --> 00:10:05,700
Perfect scores in four of five subjects.

181
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:08,450
For real? I didn't expect that.

182
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:09,420
You didn't?

183
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,480
N-Not like that!

184
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,720
I just had no idea you 
were <i>that</i> good at studying.

185
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,480
If you're in second place, then who's first?

186
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:19,960
They must have had perfect 
scores in every subject.

187
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,440
First place is Shii-kun.

188
00:10:23,150 --> 00:10:24,490
Of course he is...

189
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,340
I'll beat him in the finals!

190
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,860
<i>I'm the only one who can't study.</i>

191
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,800
Enomoto-san, can you teach me this part?

192
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:34,650
Where?

193
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,210
Umm, oh yeah.

194
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:39,440
You can solve this 
by substituting this for x.

195
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,320
Wait, maybe that's not it.

196
00:10:45,070 --> 00:10:45,920
<i>Don't look!</i>

197
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,800
A-Are you thirsty?

198
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,950
I'll get us something to drink.

199
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:05,060
<i>My heart almost stopped.</i>

200
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:09,030
<i>Unlike Himari, Enomoto-san 
does that unknowingly.</i>

201
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:12,750
<i>Himari better hurry up 
while I can still keep my cool.</i>

202
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:16,270
<i>Not that I can keep my cool 
with her, either.</i>

203
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:37,740
Upsy-daisy.

204
00:11:44,610 --> 00:11:45,560
Enomoto-san...

205
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:48,910
I couldn't help it! It was 
the scent of cherry sage!

206
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,340
Cherry sage?

207
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,350
It smelled so nice, and then I realized...

208
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:56,320
The same scent was coming 
from your bed, so...

209
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,280
Oh, that.

210
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,110
It's probably this.

211
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:03,280
I was drinking this on my bed, 
and spilled a bit of it.

212
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,520
It's cherry sage tea. Try some.

213
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,690
It smells so good.

214
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,670
That's really good!

215
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:20,980
You're right.

216
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,470
It smells like cherry sage tea.

217
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,430
That's a bit embarrassing.

218
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,900
Well... I like you, Yu-kun.

219
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,260
<i>Back when Himari and I weren't talking,</i>

220
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,960
<i>Enomoto-san confessed to me 
for the first time.</i>

221
00:12:42,490 --> 00:12:44,810
<i>I was preparing to use up all my flowers</i>

222
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:47,480
<i>so I could go to Tokyo with Himari.</i>

223
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,200
<i>It's not even like I asked for her help.</i>

224
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:52,970
<i>But before I knew it, 
she was making them with me.</i>

225
00:12:58,610 --> 00:12:59,490
I like you.

226
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,800
I've liked you for seven years.

227
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:07,760
<i>If I hadn't realized my feelings 
for Himari back then,</i>

228
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,760
<i>what would I have done?</i>

229
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:15,190
<i>Since then, Enomoto-san 
has been more direct with me.</i>

230
00:13:16,510 --> 00:13:18,240
Phew, done.

231
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,630
Now to check my answers.

232
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:23,590
<i>She's being super trusting.</i>

233
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:26,580
<i>Like the day after I turned her down.</i>

234
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:29,010
<i>She came up to me and said hi like usual.</i>

235
00:13:30,970 --> 00:13:32,910
<i>Better wake her up before Himari gets here.</i>

236
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:38,240
Enomoto-san, wake up. It's already evening.

237
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,370
W-W-Wait!

238
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:48,420
<i>How is she still asleep?!</i>

239
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:52,130
<i>She's like a real-life 
character out of a rom-com manga!</i>

240
00:13:52,130 --> 00:13:54,560
Yu! I've arrived...

241
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,350
H-Himari!

242
00:13:58,350 --> 00:13:59,690
It's not what it looks like!

243
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,120
You idiot...

244
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,300
How dare you sneak a girl into the house?

245
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:06,160
All while having a girl like Himari-chan?

246
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,840
I swear it's not!

247
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:10,960
We were studying, 
but Enomoto-san fell asleep!

248
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:15,300
Enomoto-san, you're so strong! 
How's this possible?

249
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:17,960
Wake up! I can't move!

250
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,040
It's not funny!

251
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:22,170
I'm so sorry!

252
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:26,640
Just thinking of Yu-kun sleeping here 
every night made me drift off to sleep...

253
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:30,170
So you're Kureha's little sister, huh?

254
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:33,250
Saku-nee-san, you know Enomoto-san's sister?

255
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:37,840
Know her? We were high school classmates.

256
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:43,630
We get together with Hibari-kun sometimes 
when she's back from Tokyo.

257
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,870
We met this New Year's, too.

258
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,430
With Onii-chan?

259
00:14:47,430 --> 00:14:49,140
Yup. You didn't hear?

260
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:52,120
Enocchi's sister is 
a taboo topic in our house.

261
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,380
That's no surprise from Hibari-kun.

262
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:57,830
He doesn't like to reveal his weaknesses.

263
00:14:57,830 --> 00:14:58,830
But still...

264
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,690
I'm surprised they don't fight.

265
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:03,970
Well they're adults, unlike you guys.

266
00:15:04,350 --> 00:15:06,210
My sister can be a bit odd.

267
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:09,840
So I didn't know she had friends back home.

268
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,960
Thank you for taking care of her.

269
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:15,600
So, Rion-chan was it?

270
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:18,600
You don't actually like my idiot brother—

271
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,670
Seriously?

272
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:26,270
You're so cute, but you 
have awful taste in guys.

273
00:15:26,270 --> 00:15:27,990
Just like Kureha.

274
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:35,820
Sorry about Saku-nee-san.

275
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,410
I think she's a great older sister.

276
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:40,040
You do?

277
00:15:40,490 --> 00:15:41,780
She's better than my sister,

278
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:45,620
who came back during New Year's 
but couldn't be bothered

279
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:47,800
to give any of us family members a heads up.

280
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,880
Okay...

281
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,530
But you know...

282
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:52,200
Just something I noticed.

283
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,930
Neither of you seemed too 
bothered by Sakura-san teasing you.

284
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,200
Enomoto-san confessed 
to me during our fight.

285
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,520
Wh-What?!

286
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:07,020
And you still tried to go to Tokyo with me?

287
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:07,940
What's wrong with you?

288
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:09,920
Well, I turned her down.

289
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:13,300
B-But you've both been so normal.

290
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:15,800
Isn't that usually an awkward situation?

291
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:18,180
She's actually confessed 
three times already.

292
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,050
Three times?

293
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:21,160
If I count that last one, four times.

294
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:25,600
J-Just now? All while I was gone?

295
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,330
Yes, I did.

296
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:31,300
Yu, what the heck?!

297
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,940
Taking advantage of Enocchi 
and keeping her around?

298
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,950
That's not like you!

299
00:16:35,950 --> 00:16:39,240
Um, well I turn her down every time.

300
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:43,780
But it's always business as usual 
the next day, and she bakes me cookies.

301
00:16:44,110 --> 00:16:46,900
Don't get lured in by cookies!

302
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:48,060
H-Hey Himari, calm down.

303
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,680
You can't be wishy washy like that!

304
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,950
Even if she is your first crush!

305
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:54,050
First crush?

306
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,000
Yu-kun, is that true?

307
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,240
Himari!

308
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:59,360
Why are you exposing me like that?

309
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:01,290
I'm sorry!

310
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:08,290
You're my first crush, but I'm not sure 
if that means I like you now.

311
00:17:08,810 --> 00:17:12,800
And I can't accept your offer 
just because you're pretty.

312
00:17:13,510 --> 00:17:14,480
Yu-kun...

313
00:17:17,490 --> 00:17:19,650
Gotcha! Good to know for next time!

314
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:20,660
What was that memo?

315
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,880
Man, you're optimistic.

316
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:24,020
Anyways, what about you two?

317
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:26,520
You seemed awkward until this morning.

318
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,920
Oh yeah! Hmph!

319
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,240
That's not very convincing.

320
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,840
I totally forgot.

321
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:34,730
I wasn't supposed to talk to Hii-chan.

322
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:35,940
You weren't?

323
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:37,260
From a couple days ago.

324
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,030
She messaged me.

325
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,410
That didn't last long.

326
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:44,040
Enomoto-san, you forgot after 
the whole study group thing, didn't you?

327
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:47,200
Because Hii-chan said she supported me.

328
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,770
Then she went and tried 
to take you to Tokyo.

329
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:53,460
I guess that's partly my fault, too.

330
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:56,930
But I know that I don't deserve 
to get mad over that.

331
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:03,720
Shii-kun told me that I shouldn't complain 
until I've worked hard to be number one.

332
00:18:04,010 --> 00:18:07,340
Hii-chan's worked two years 
to be Yu-kun's number one.

333
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,720
I haven't worked at all in seven years.

334
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:12,210
I have no right to criticize Hii-chan.

335
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:17,480
That's why I'll become both Yu-kun 
and Hii-chan's number one!

336
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:18,440
Come again?

337
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:24,820
If I become Yu-kun's number one 
and Hii-chan's number one friend,

338
00:18:25,290 --> 00:18:26,700
everything works out, right?

339
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:30,480
<i>So she would feel bad 
coming between Himari and me,</i>

340
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:33,770
<i>so instead, she's gonna 
take both of us for herself?</i>

341
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:37,080
<i>Is this a threat? What kind of 
wartime general is she?</i>

342
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,920
Uh, Enomoto-san...

343
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:43,780
After thinking about it, Hii-chan's 
worked really hard as the main model.

344
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:46,890
So I should respect that role as hers.

345
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:49,350
U-Um, thanks.

346
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:51,770
Besides, if I'm gonna work hard for Yu-kun,

347
00:18:51,770 --> 00:18:53,680
I can't just copy her.

348
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:56,890
That's why I was hoping 
to help you behind the scenes.

349
00:18:56,890 --> 00:18:57,610
What do you think?

350
00:18:59,830 --> 00:19:01,170
If you're okay with that.

351
00:19:01,990 --> 00:19:05,580
Yay! That works better for me anyways
since I have club after school.

352
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:08,600
If I learn more about 
online orders and shipping,

353
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,540
I bet I can help out more 
with my family's cake shop, too!

354
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:13,000
Well if that's the case, great.

355
00:19:13,410 --> 00:19:16,160
Enocchi's stubborn when she gets like this.

356
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:17,760
I think it's a great idea.

357
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:21,840
Then we'd love to work with you!

358
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,660
Great! I'll do my best!

359
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:26,300
Let's celebrate the new You team!

360
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:37,420
You do realize what you just did, right?

361
00:19:37,690 --> 00:19:40,250
Letting Enomoto's little sister join you.

362
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,830
It couldn't be helped.

363
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:45,080
She was so sincere about us being friends.

364
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:50,040
<i>Honestly, I know I did 
a terrible thing by telling her</i>

365
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,570
<i>I'd support her then going behind her back.</i>

366
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:57,310
Onii-chan, I heard you still 
hang out with Kureha-san.

367
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:58,760
Sakura-kun told you?

368
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:01,630
She always lets things slip.

369
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,590
You're still not over her?

370
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:07,060
Never mind me, worry about yourself.

371
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:08,100
Why?

372
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:12,280
Not only did you mistake the balance 
between friendship and romance,

373
00:20:12,630 --> 00:20:15,730
you chose the wrong partner 
to create accessories with.

374
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:21,950
First, your emotions got the best of you,
and Yu-kun had to retake his exams.

375
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:26,320
Now, you're holding Yu-kun back under 
the guise of being his best friend.

376
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:31,460
If you can't help each other be better, 
you have no right to stand beside him.

377
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:37,760
It's not like Yu-kun's dream 
depends on your support.

378
00:20:38,210 --> 00:20:41,460
I could just adopt him 
into the Inuzuka family.

379
00:20:41,730 --> 00:20:45,210
Onii-chan, you never think 
about anyone besides Yu.

380
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,930
So? What am I supposed to do now?

381
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:52,840
Stop lying to Yu-kun.

382
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:53,850
Lying?

383
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:57,470
You have a habit of preparing 
an escape route.

384
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:03,320
Until you fix that, you'll lose to Enomoto's 
sister and never be Yu-kun's equal.

385
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:07,780
I understand. I accept that challenge.

386
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:09,830
Very well then.

387
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:12,100
How about some treats on the way home?

388
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,250
Really?

389
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:19,790
It's my fault for not being able to 
let Enomoto's sister in our house.

390
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,380
Buy whatever you'd like.

391
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,570
Thanks, Onii-chan!

392
00:21:23,570 --> 00:21:26,220
Then I want some ice cream
or black Mont Blanc!

393
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,190
Oh yeah, Onii-chan.

394
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:31,860
About the no lying thing, 
what's considered a lie?

395
00:21:34,050 --> 00:21:38,210
Himari! That's the problem with you!

396
00:21:35,930 --> 00:21:37,920
I'm sorry! I didn't mean to!

397
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:40,240
It was a reflex!

398
00:21:40,250 --> 00:21:45,560
That kind of thoughtless banter 
risks Yu-kun losing his cool!

399
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:46,980
I understand!

400
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:52,360
I'll be an honest person 
so I can be Yu's equal!

401
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,950
Exam Retake Day

402
00:21:54,210 --> 00:21:54,950
See?

403
00:21:55,330 --> 00:21:58,410
If you can get a perfect score, 
do the work to begin with!

404
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,920
Sorry about that!

405
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:03,890
<i>Thankfully, I got 
by without having to quit high school.</i>

406
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:39,890
The Cracked Crocus

